### 2.1 Input Modalities

The input 𝐱\mathbf{x} aggregates heterogeneous signals that describe the external environment and the ego-vehicle state [[17](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib17), [233](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib233), [270](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib270)]. These inputs can be grouped into four categories: sensor observations, latent scene representations, language instructions, and proprioceptive states.

𝐱\mathbf{x}

#### 2.1.2 Latent Representations

Multiple VLA systems operate on intermediate spatial representations that fuse multimodal sensor inputs.

* • Bird’s-Eye View (BEV) Features. Top-down view representation, often generated by fusing camera or LiDAR data [[150](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib150), [155](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib155), [168](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib168)]: 𝐱bev∈ℝC×Hbev×Wbev\mathbf{x}\_{\mathrm{bev}}\in\mathbb{R}^{C\times H\_{\mathrm{bev}}\times W\_{\mathrm{bev}}}, where CC is the number of feature channels, and Hbev,WbevH\_{\mathrm{bev}},W\_{\mathrm{bev}} are the spatial dimensions of the BEV grid. * • Occupancy Grids. 3D volumetric representation predicting occupancy and semantics for each spatial location [[260](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib260), [268](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib268), [284](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib284), [167](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib167)]: 𝐱occ∈ℝCocc×X×Y×Z\mathbf{x}\_{\mathrm{occ}}\in\mathbb{R}^{C\_{\mathrm{occ}}\times X\times Y\times Z}, where X,Y,ZX,Y,Z are the spatial resolution of the 3D grid, and CoccC\_{\mathrm{occ}} denotes the number of occupancy feature channels (*e.g.*, occupancy, flow and semantics).

