#### 2.1.3 Language Inputs

To enable VLA capabilities, the model also receives high-level textual instructions or task descriptions [[66](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib66), [287](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib287), [76](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2512.16760v2#bib.bib76)]. It is composed of a sequence of tokens representing the driving task or goal (*e.g.*, *“turn left at the next intersection”*): 𝐱lang∈ℤT\mathbf{x}\_{\mathrm{lang}}\in\mathbb{Z}^{T} or 𝐱lang∈ℝT×Demb\mathbf{x}\_{\mathrm{lang}}\in\mathbb{R}^{T\times D\_{\mathrm{emb}}}, where TT is the sequence length, and DembD\_{\mathrm{emb}} is the embedding dimension (if token embeddings are used).

